2026-11-11 - Change Notes:
  - Fix ecommerce: GA4 ecommerce events are sent as Piwik PRO ecommerce events (e_t + ec_products)
  - Add Ecommerce, Custom Dimensions & Variables and User Configuration sections
  - Deprecate Auth Token: no longer required to send the visitor IP (cip)
  - Normalize Visitor ID and pv_id to the API formats; forward x-pp-* event data
  - Send object/array values as JSON; add cur, search_cats, lon and r parameters
  - Handle Tracking URLs without a trailing slash; an empty Tracking URL fails the tag
  - Skip GTM measurement requests (standard Stape shouldExitEarly checks)
  - Send hits with a query string over 2048 characters as POST with a JSON body
  - Bump version to sgtm_stape 1.1.0
  - Potential breaking changes:
    - Ecommerce events no longer send idgoal=0, ec_items or custom event params; page views no longer send idgoal=0 (Custom setups keep it)
    - Page views no longer send e_n=page_view
    - Visitor IP is sent without an Auth Token
    - Non-hex Visitor IDs are hashed and the _pk_ cookie rewritten (counted as new visitors once); pv_id values change
    - idgoal, uia, rmip, _cvar and x-pp-* are forwarded from event data; _rcn wins over affiliation, ec_st over value
    - Long hits use POST (custom Content-Type ignored); new read_request permission (referer)

